# SMILES  name
# The acetyltropine story: the compound itself, its alcohol, and a related root ester.
CN1[C@H]2CC[C@@H]1C[C@@H](OC(C)=O)C2	acetyltropine
CN1[C@H]2CC[C@@H]1C[C@@H](O)C2	tropine
C/C=C(\C)/C(=O)OC1C[C@H]2CC[C@@H](C1)N2C	3-tigloyloxytropane
# Known muscarinic ligands, as a yardstick. Tiotropium is the 5CXV crystal ligand and is the
# redocking control; it is a quaternary ammonium already, so prep.py leaves its charge alone.
C[N+]1(C)[C@H]2C[C@@H](C[C@@H]1[C@H]1O[C@@H]21)OC(=O)C(O)(c1cccs1)c1cccs1	tiotropium
CN1[C@H]2CC[C@@H]1C[C@@H](C2)OC(=O)C(CO)c1ccccc1	atropine
CN1[C@H]2C[C@@H](C[C@@H]1[C@H]1O[C@@H]21)OC(=O)C(CO)c1ccccc1	scopolamine
COC(=O)[C@H]1[C@@H](OC(=O)c2ccccc2)C[C@@H]2CC[C@H]1N2C	cocaine
